{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/waitset.cljc; nl -ba test/dao/stream/waitset_test.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.waitset\n     2\t  \"The multiplexed wait-set for DaoStream: one complete ordered sweep over\n     3\t  every parked waiter, as a host-agnostic library.\n     4\t\n     5\t  The waitset is a value, `{:waiting []}`, and it holds only what waits.\n     6\t  `check` takes it beside a host-composed resolver and the host's store,\n     7\t  performs one synchronous interpreter step — polling live media, appending\n     8\t  for a parked writer — and returns the successor waitset beside that\n     9\t  call's results. The sweep has explicit stream effects, so it is never\n    10\t  described as pure; what is immutable is the threading of the store and\n    11\t  the waitset.\n    12\t\n    13\t  Entries are the host's data. The library interprets only `:reason` —\n    14\t  `:next` reads, `:put` appends — and every other field is opaque, stored\n    15\t  and returned exactly as the host gave it. A resolver maps each whole\n    16\t  entry to a live handle and the cursor to read from or the value to\n    17\t  append, and moves a reader's cursor in the store; both functions run\n    18\t  immediately inside `check` and are never retained, and the library never\n    19\t  adds a resolved handle or polling cursor to any entry.\n    20\t\n    21\t  Woken entries are returned, never dispatched: no callbacks, no queues,\n    22\t  no disposition functions. This namespace multiplexes readiness; it does\n    23\t  not schedule work — the host loop owns everything between calls.\"\n    24\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]))\n    25\t\n    26\t\n    27\t(def ^:private wait-reasons\n    28\t  \"The reasons the library interprets. Only two outcomes can change on\n    29\t   their own: `blocked` for a reader, `full` for a writer.\"\n    30\t  #{:next :put})\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\t(defn empty-waitset\n    34\t  \"The waitset that parks nothing. This value is the whole threaded state.\"\n    35\t  []\n    36\t  {:waiting []})\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t(defn park\n    40\t  \"Append `entry` to `waitset`'s `:waiting` and return the successor\n    41\t   waitset. Total: it rejects nothing, because `check` classifies\n    42\t   everything — a malformed entry is woken by the sweep as a diagnostic,\n    43\t   never a park-time error. Total over the waitset it is handed too: a\n    44\t   missing or nil `:waiting` parks onto a fresh vector, so park order —\n    45\t   wake order among co-waiters — is preserved whatever the host threaded.\"\n    46\t  [waitset entry]\n    47\t  (update waitset :waiting (fnil conj []) entry))\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\t(defn- woken-result\n    51\t  \"The result map for one woken entry: the stored entry verbatim beside\n    52\t   the status its poll resolved with. `cursor` is present only when the\n    53\t   poll produced one — a reader's successor or a gap's recovery position;\n    54\t   a writer resolves with no cursor.\"\n    55\t  [entry status value cursor]\n    56\t  (cond-> {:entry entry :status status :value value}\n    57\t    cursor (assoc :cursor cursor)))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t(defn- diagnostic-result\n    61\t  \"The result map for an entry the library cannot poll at all: the stored\n    62\t   entry verbatim and its qualified status. No stream operation was\n    63\t   performed, so there is no value.\"\n    64\t  [entry status]\n    65\t  {:entry entry :status status})\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\t(defn- answer-defect\n    69\t  \"Why `answer` cannot be interpreted as an outcome of `op`, or nil when it\n    70\t   can, using the contract's own validation. `:invalid` marks an answer\n    71\t   that is not an outcome map the contract can vouch for — a non-map, a\n    72\t   missing or unqualified `:dao.stream/outcome`, or a declared outcome\n    73\t   missing its required keys — which folds into the waitset's own\n    74\t   diagnostic. `:unauthorized` marks a well-formed outcome outside the\n    75\t   operation's declared set, which stays terminal under its own keyword\n    76\t   (the plan's rule for undeclared outcomes) and is distinguished here so\n    77\t   it does not collide with the fold.\"\n    78\t  [op answer]\n    79\t  (let [defect (stream/validate-outcome op answer)]\n    80\t    (cond\n    81\t      (nil? defect) nil\n    82\t      (= :unauthorized-outcome (:error defect)) :unauthorized\n    83\t      :else :invalid)))\n    84\t\n    85\t\n    86\t(defn- poll-next\n    87\t  \"Poll one resolved `:next` entry with a synchronous read. Returns nil\n    88\t   while the entry must keep waiting — `blocked` is the only reader\n    89\t   outcome that can change on its own — and otherwise the woken result\n    90\t   plus `:advance-cursor`, the position the store must move to before\n    91\t   later entries resolve: the successor on `ok`, the recovery position on\n    92\t   `gap`. `end` resolves as the immediate path yields it, and every other\n    93\t   outcome — cursor-mismatch, invalid-cursor, transport-error, and\n    94\t   anything undeclared — is terminal under its own keyword.\n    95\t\n    96\t   An answer that is not an outcome map the contract can vouch for — a\n    97\t   non-map, a missing or unqualified outcome, a declared outcome missing\n    98\t   its required keys — folds into the qualified terminal status\n    99\t   `:dao.stream.waitset/invalid-answer` instead of waking as an\n   100\t   unnameable `:status nil`. A poll that throws — a `:stream` that fails\n   101\t   its protocol, a defective transport — folds into the same diagnostic:\n   102\t   the entry cannot be trusted to poll again, and an uninterpretable\n   103\t   answer is terminal data, never an exception and never a wait.\"\n   104\t  [entry resolved]\n   105\t  (try\n   106\t    (let [result (stream/next (:stream resolved) (:cursor resolved))\n   107\t          o (:dao.stream/outcome result)]\n   108\t      (if (= :invalid (answer-defect :next result))\n   109\t        {:wake (diagnostic-result entry :dao.stream.waitset/invalid-answer)}\n   110\t        (case o\n   111\t          :dao.stream/ok\n   112\t          (let [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result)]\n   113\t            {:wake (woken-result entry :ok (:dao.stream/value result) cursor)\n   114\t             :advance-cursor cursor})\n   115\t\n   116\t          :dao.stream/blocked nil\n   117\t\n   118\t          :dao.stream/end\n   119\t          {:wake (woken-result entry :end nil nil)}\n   120\t\n   121\t          :dao.stream/gap\n   122\t          (let [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result)]\n   123\t            {:wake (woken-result entry :dao.stream/gap :dao.stream/gap cursor)\n   124\t             :advance-cursor cursor})\n   125\t\n   126\t          ;; Terminal under its own keyword, never a wait: waiting on an\n   127\t          ;; answer the library cannot interpret would spin.\n   128\t          {:wake (woken-result entry o o nil)})))\n   129\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   130\t      {:wake (diagnostic-result entry :dao.stream.waitset/invalid-answer)})))\n   131\t\n   132\t\n   133\t(defn- poll-put\n   134\t  \"Poll one resolved `:put` entry by appending — the append is an effect\n   135\t   of this poll, and `check` returns the state that records it. Returns\n   136\t   nil while the entry must keep waiting — `full` is the only writer\n   137\t   outcome that can change on its own — and otherwise the woken result.\n   138\t   `ok` resolves with the appended value and no cursor; `closed` is a\n   139\t   terminal append failure under its own keyword, never a reader's `end`;\n   140\t   every other outcome, declared or not, is terminal under its own\n   141\t   keyword.\n   142\t\n   143\t   A resolution with no `:value` appends nil: the transport is the one\n   144\t   that answers `invalid-value`, and the engine reads its `:datom` the\n   145\t   same loose way. An answer that is not an outcome map, and a poll that\n   146\t   throws — a `:stream` failing its writer protocol, a defective\n   147\t   transport — fold into `:dao.stream.waitset/invalid-answer`, exactly as\n   148\t   the reader's poll does: the entry cannot be trusted to poll again.\"\n   149\t  [entry resolved]\n   150\t  (try\n   151\t    (let [value (:value resolved)\n   152\t          result (stream/append! (:stream resolved) value)\n   153\t          o (:dao.stream/outcome result)]\n   154\t      (if (= :invalid (answer-defect :append! result))\n   155\t        {:wake (diagnostic-result entry :dao.stream.waitset/invalid-answer)}\n   156\t        (case o\n   157\t          :dao.stream/ok {:wake (woken-result entry :ok value nil)}\n   158\t          :dao.stream/full nil\n   159\t          {:wake (woken-result entry o o nil)})))\n   160\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   161\t      {:wake (diagnostic-result entry :dao.stream.waitset/invalid-answer)})))\n   162\t\n   163\t\n   164\t(defn check\n   165\t  \"Run one complete ordered sweep over `waitset`'s entries: a synchronous,\n   166\t  state-threaded interpreter step with explicit stream effects — it calls\n   167\t  `next` on live media and a parked writer's `append!` — so it is never\n   168\t  described as pure.\n   169\t\n   170\t  `resolver` is host composition, two synchronous functions over whole\n   171\t  entries:\n   172\t\n   173\t    {:resolve (fn [store entry] ...)          ; => {:stream h :cursor c :value v} or nil\n   174\t     :advance (fn [store entry cursor] ...)}  ; => store'\n   175\t\n   176\t  `:resolve` maps an entry to its live handle plus the cursor to read from\n   177\t  (`:next`) or the value to append (`:put`), or answers nil when it\n   178\t  cannot. `:advance` returns the store with that entry's reader cursor\n   179\t  moved to `cursor`. Both are invoked immediately, per entry, and never\n   180\t  retained — the shape of `reduce`'s `f`, not an event callback. The store\n   181\t  is opaque to this library: it is never dereferenced here, only passed\n   182\t  through.\n   183\t\n   184\t  Returns\n   185\t\n   186\t    {:waitset {:waiting [...]}   ; thread this into the next check\n   187\t     :woken   [...]              ; this call's results only; host-owned\n   188\t     :store   store'}            ; the host commits this\n   189\t\n   190\t  Every entry is polled every call, one at a time in wait-set order — no\n   191\t  budget, no scan position. A still-waiting entry (`blocked` for a reader,\n   192\t  `full` for a writer) is retained exactly as stored. A resolved entry\n   193\t  leaves `:waiting` and appears in `:woken` as\n   194\t\n   195\t    {:entry <the stored entry> :status ... :value ... :cursor ...}\n   196\t\n   197\t  where `:cursor` is present only for a reader whose poll returned one.\n   198\t  The library never adds a resolved handle or polling cursor to any entry\n   199\t  it retains or returns, and `:woken` never accumulates: check the\n   200\t  returned `:waitset` again and it answers only what moved since.\n   201\t\n   202\t  Two laws are preserved from the engine this sweep generalizes.\n   203\t  Shared-cursor write-back: a woken reader's successor — or recovery\n   204\t  cursor, on gap — is advanced in the store before later entries resolve,\n   205\t  so co-waiters on one cursor read distinct values and a co-waiter behind\n   206\t  a gap reads from the recovery position; wait-set order is therefore wake\n   207\t  order, and nothing reorders `:waiting`. A parked writer retries by\n   208\t  appending: the append is an effect of the poll, so no caller may drop a\n   209\t  returned `:waitset` or `:store`.\n   210\t\n   211\t  Classification is total, per operation. For a `:next` entry only\n   212\t  `blocked` waits: `ok` resolves with the value and its successor, `end`\n   213\t  as `{:value nil :status :end}`, `gap` with its recovery cursor, and\n   214\t  cursor-mismatch, invalid-cursor and transport-error under their own\n   215\t  qualified keywords. For a `:put` entry only `full` waits: `ok` resolves\n   216\t  with the appended value and no cursor; closed, invalid-value and\n   217\t  transport-error are terminal append failures under their own keywords —\n   218\t  writer `closed` is never a reader's `end`. Any outcome outside the\n   219\t  operation's declared set is terminal under its own keyword, never a\n   220\t  wait.\n   221\t\n   222\t  Three diagnostics are the library's own, and they also never wait: an\n   223\t  entry whose `:resolve` answers nil or without a `:stream` wakes with\n   224\t  `:status :dao.stream.waitset/unresolved`; an entry whose `:reason` is\n   225\t  neither `:next` nor `:put` wakes with\n   226\t  `:status :dao.stream.waitset/unsupported-reason`; and a poll that\n   227\t  answers something other than an outcome map — or throws, because its\n   228\t  handle fails the protocol it was resolved to — wakes with\n   229\t  `:status :dao.stream.waitset/invalid-answer`, the entry no longer\n   230\t  being one that can be trusted to poll. In every case no `:advance` is\n   231\t  called, the store is unchanged, the original entry is returned intact,\n   232\t  and the entry leaves `:waiting`.\n   233\t\n   234\t  Resolvers must not throw. A resolver throw voids the sweep: `check`\n   235\t  does not return, and a caller that re-threads its previous waitset\n   236\t  into a later call re-polls every entry — re-appending writers that\n   237\t  already appended. The engine's sweep behaves identically, and this is\n   238\t  stated as the contract on resolvers rather than caught: host\n   239\t  composition failing is a host defect the library cannot name, and\n   240\t  wrapping it would hide it inside a diagnostic.\"\n   241\t  [waitset resolver store]\n   242\t  (let [{resolve-fn :resolve, advance-fn :advance} resolver]\n   243\t    (loop [remaining (:waiting waitset)\n   244\t           store store\n   245\t           waiting []\n   246\t           woken []]\n   247\t      (if (seq remaining)\n   248\t        (let [entry (first remaining)\n   249\t              reason (:reason entry)]\n   250\t          (if (contains? wait-reasons reason)\n   251\t            (let [resolved (resolve-fn store entry)]\n   252\t              (if (and (map? resolved) (:stream resolved))\n   253\t                (if-some [{:keys [wake advance-cursor]}\n   254\t                          (case reason\n   255\t                            :next (poll-next entry resolved)\n   256\t                            :put (poll-put entry resolved))]\n   257\t                  (recur (rest remaining)\n   258\t                         (cond-> store\n   259\t                           advance-cursor (advance-fn entry advance-cursor))\n   260\t                         waiting\n   261\t                         (conj woken wake))\n   262\t                  (recur (rest remaining)\n   263\t                         store\n   264\t                         (conj waiting entry)\n   265\t                         woken))\n   266\t                (recur (rest remaining)\n   267\t                       store\n   268\t                       waiting\n   269\t                       (conj woken (diagnostic-result\n   270\t                                    entry\n   271\t                                    :dao.stream.waitset/unresolved)))))\n   272\t            (recur (rest remaining)\n   273\t                   store\n   274\t                   waiting\n   275\t                   (conj woken (diagnostic-result\n   276\t                                entry\n   277\t                                :dao.stream.waitset/unsupported-reason)))))\n   278\t        {:waitset {:waiting waiting}\n   279\t         :woken woken\n   280\t         :store store}))))\n     1\t(ns dao.stream.waitset-test\n     2\t  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]\n     3\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n     4\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n     5\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n     6\t            [dao.stream.waitset :as waitset]))\n     7\t\n     8\t\n     9\t(def ring-spec\n    10\t  {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n    11\t   :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity 8})\n    12\t\n    13\t\n    14\t(defn ring-handle\n    15\t  \"A fresh v2 ring buffer of `capacity`.\"\n    16\t  ([]\n    17\t   (:dao.stream/handle (ring/create! ring-spec)))\n    18\t  ([capacity]\n    19\t   (:dao.stream/handle (ring/create! (assoc ring-spec\n    20\t                                            ring/capacity-key capacity)))))\n    21\t\n    22\t\n    23\t(defn cursor\n    24\t  [h anchor]\n    25\t  (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h anchor)))\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    29\t;; The store: an association list of [ref binding] pairs, keyed by host refs\n    30\t;; the library has never heard of — not the VM's map of {:id …} records.\n    31\t;; Each binding carries a handle and the host's current cursor for that ref.\n    32\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    33\t\n    34\t(defn alist-store\n    35\t  \"Build the store from {ref [handle cursor]} bindings.\"\n    36\t  [bindings]\n    37\t  (mapv (fn [[ref [handle cursor]]]\n    38\t          [ref {:handle handle :cursor cursor}])\n    39\t        bindings))\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\t(defn alist-fetch\n    43\t  [store ref]\n    44\t  (some (fn [[r binding]] (when (= r ref) binding)) store))\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t(defn alist-cursor\n    48\t  [store ref]\n    49\t  (:cursor (alist-fetch store ref)))\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(defn alist-advance\n    53\t  \"Move one ref's cursor and return the successor store.\"\n    54\t  [store ref cursor]\n    55\t  (mapv (fn [[r binding]]\n    56\t          (if (= r ref)\n    57\t            [r (assoc binding :cursor cursor)]\n    58\t            [r binding]))\n    59\t        store))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(defn alist-resolver\n    63\t  []\n    64\t  {:resolve (fn [store entry]\n    65\t              (when-let [binding (alist-fetch store (:my/ref entry))]\n    66\t                {:stream (:handle binding)\n    67\t                 :cursor (:cursor binding)\n    68\t                 :value (:my/value entry)}))\n    69\t   :advance (fn [store entry cursor]\n    70\t              (alist-advance store (:my/ref entry) cursor))})\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\t(defn counting-reader\n    74\t  \"A reader that counts its `next` calls and always answers `blocked`.\"\n    75\t  []\n    76\t  (let [calls (atom 0)]\n    77\t    {:calls calls\n    78\t     :handle (reify stream/IDaoStreamReader\n    79\t               (next [_ _]\n    80\t                 (swap! calls inc)\n    81\t                 {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))}))\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t(defn scripted-reader\n    85\t  \"A reader whose `next` answers `outcome` with the keys the contract\n    86\t   requires of it, and counts its calls.\"\n    87\t  [outcome]\n    88\t  (let [calls (atom 0)]\n    89\t    {:calls calls\n    90\t     :handle (reify stream/IDaoStreamReader\n    91\t               (next [_ _]\n    92\t                 (swap! calls inc)\n    93\t                 (case outcome\n    94\t                   :dao.stream/ok {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n    95\t                                   :dao.stream/value :sent\n    96\t                                   :dao.stream/cursor {:pos 1}}\n    97\t                   :dao.stream/gap {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/gap\n    98\t                                    :dao.stream/cursor {:pos 7}}\n    99\t                   {:dao.stream/outcome outcome})))}))\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\t(defn scripted-writer\n   103\t  \"A writer whose `append!` always answers `outcome`, and counts its\n   104\t   calls.\"\n   105\t  [outcome]\n   106\t  (let [calls (atom 0)]\n   107\t    {:calls calls\n   108\t     :handle (reify stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   109\t               (append! [_ _]\n   110\t                 (swap! calls inc)\n   111\t                 {:dao.stream/outcome outcome}))}))\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\t(defn full-once-writer\n   115\t  \"A writer whose first append answers `full` and whose later appends\n   116\t   answer `ok`; counts every append.\"\n   117\t  []\n   118\t  (let [calls (atom 0)]\n   119\t    {:calls calls\n   120\t     :handle (reify stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   121\t               (append! [_ _]\n   122\t                 (if (= 1 (swap! calls inc))\n   123\t                   {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/full}\n   124\t                   {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})))}))\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn answering-reader\n   128\t  \"A reader whose `next` returns `answer` verbatim — a fixture for answers\n   129\t   that are not outcome maps at all. Counts its calls.\"\n   130\t  [answer]\n   131\t  (let [calls (atom 0)]\n   132\t    {:calls calls\n   133\t     :handle (reify stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   134\t               (next [_ _]\n   135\t                 (swap! calls inc)\n   136\t                 answer))}))\n   137\t\n   138\t\n   139\t(defn answering-writer\n   140\t  \"A writer whose `append!` returns `answer` verbatim; counts its calls.\"\n   141\t  [answer]\n   142\t  (let [calls (atom 0)]\n   143\t    {:calls calls\n   144\t     :handle (reify stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   145\t               (append! [_ _]\n   146\t                 (swap! calls inc)\n   147\t                 answer))}))\n   148\t\n   149\t\n   150\t(defn fixture-resolver\n   151\t  \"Resolve every entry to `handle`; a fixture for the reified-handle\n   152\t   suites. `advances` counts the sweep's write-backs.\"\n   153\t  [handle advances]\n   154\t  {:resolve (fn [_store _entry]\n   155\t              {:stream handle :cursor {:pos 0} :value :payload})\n   156\t   :advance (fn [store _entry _cursor]\n   157\t              (swap! advances inc)\n   158\t              store)})\n   159\t\n   160\t\n   161\t(defn check-one\n   162\t  \"Park `entry` alone, resolve it to `handle`, and sweep once. Returns the\n   163\t   check's result beside the number of `:advance` calls it made, so the\n   164\t   classification loops can pin the write-back count per outcome.\"\n   165\t  [entry handle]\n   166\t  (let [advances (atom 0)\n   167\t        check (waitset/check (waitset/park (waitset/empty-waitset) entry)\n   168\t                             (fixture-resolver handle advances)\n   169\t                             [])]\n   170\t    {:check check :advances @advances}))\n   171\t\n   172\t\n   173\t(def next-outcome-plan\n   174\t  \"Literal classification for a `:next` entry: the status the woken result\n   175\t   carries, or `:wait` — the only reader outcome that can change on its\n   176\t   own. The key set is pinned to `dao.stream/outcomes-next`, so a future\n   177\t   contract outcome fails here on domain inequality instead of passing\n   178\t   through a default branch.\"\n   179\t  {:dao.stream/ok :ok\n   180\t   :dao.stream/blocked :wait\n   181\t   :dao.stream/end :end\n   182\t   :dao.stream/gap :dao.stream/gap\n   183\t   :dao.stream/cursor-mismatch :dao.stream/cursor-mismatch\n   184\t   :dao.stream/invalid-cursor :dao.stream/invalid-cursor\n   185\t   :dao.stream/transport-error :dao.stream/transport-error})\n   186\t\n   187\t\n   188\t(def put-outcome-plan\n   189\t  \"Literal classification for a `:put` entry, pinned to\n   190\t   `dao.stream/outcomes-append`. `closed` is a terminal append failure —\n   191\t   never a reader's `end`.\"\n   192\t  {:dao.stream/ok :ok\n   193\t   :dao.stream/full :wait\n   194\t   :dao.stream/invalid-value :dao.stream/invalid-value\n   195\t   :dao.stream/closed :dao.stream/closed\n   196\t   :dao.stream/transport-error :dao.stream/transport-error})\n   197\t\n   198\t\n   199\t(deftest classification-is-pinned-per-operation\n   200\t  (testing \"the literal plans cover exactly the contract outcome sets\"\n   201\t    (is (= stream/outcomes-next (set (keys next-outcome-plan))))\n   202\t    (is (= stream/outcomes-append (set (keys put-outcome-plan)))))\n   203\t  (testing \"for a :next entry, exactly blocked waits\"\n   204\t    (doseq [[outcome status] next-outcome-plan]\n   205\t      (let [entry {:reason :next :my/ref :r}\n   206\t            {:keys [check advances]} (check-one entry\n   207\t                                                (:handle (scripted-reader\n   208\t                                                          outcome)))\n   209\t            result check]\n   210\t        (if (= :wait status)\n   211\t          (do (is (= [] (:woken result)) (str outcome \" must wait\"))\n   212\t              (is (= [entry] (get-in result [:waitset :waiting]))\n   213\t                  (str outcome \" must stay parked as stored\")))\n   214\t          (do (is (= 1 (count (:woken result))) (str outcome \" must wake\"))\n   215\t              (is (= status (:status (first (:woken result)))))\n   216\t              (is (= [] (get-in result [:waitset :waiting])))))\n   217\t        ;; The write-back happens only when the poll returned a cursor:\n   218\t        ;; the successor on ok, the recovery position on gap.\n   219\t        (is (= (if (contains? #{:dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/gap} outcome) 1 0)\n   220\t               advances)\n   221\t            (str outcome \" advance count\")))))\n   222\t  (testing \"for a :put entry, exactly full waits\"\n   223\t    (doseq [[outcome status] put-outcome-plan]\n   224\t      (let [entry {:reason :put :my/ref :r :my/value :payload}\n   225\t            {:keys [check advances]} (check-one entry\n   226\t                                                (:handle (scripted-writer\n   227\t                                                          outcome)))\n   228\t            result check]\n   229\t        (if (= :wait status)\n   230\t          (do (is (= [] (:woken result)) (str outcome \" must wait\"))\n   231\t              (is (= [entry] (get-in result [:waitset :waiting]))\n   232\t                  (str outcome \" must stay parked as stored\")))\n   233\t          (do (is (= 1 (count (:woken result))) (str outcome \" must wake\"))\n   234\t              (is (= status (:status (first (:woken result)))))\n   235\t              (is (= [] (get-in result [:waitset :waiting])))))\n   236\t        ;; A writer's poll never moves the store.\n   237\t        (is (zero? advances) (str outcome \" advance count\"))))))\n   238\t\n   239\t\n   240\t(deftest invalid-answers-fold-into-a-qualified-terminal-diagnostic\n   241\t  (testing \"a map answer with no outcome key\"\n   242\t    (let [entry {:reason :next :my/ref :r}\n   243\t          {:keys [handle calls]} (answering-reader {:dao.stream/value :sent})\n   244\t          {:keys [check advances]} (check-one entry handle)\n   245\t          wake (first (:woken check))]\n   246\t      (is (= 1 @calls) \"the poll was attempted once\")\n   247\t      (is (= 1 (count (:woken check))))\n   248\t      (is (= entry (:entry wake)))\n   249\t      (is (= :dao.stream.waitset/invalid-answer (:status wake)))\n   250\t      (is (= [] (get-in check [:waitset :waiting])))\n   251\t      (is (= [] (:store check)))\n   252\t      (is (zero? advances) \"no cursor was interpretable, so no write-back\")))\n   253\t  (testing \"a non-map answer\"\n   254\t    (let [entry {:reason :next :my/ref :r}\n   255\t          {:keys [handle calls]} (answering-reader :not-a-map)\n   256\t          {:keys [check advances]} (check-one entry handle)]\n   257\t      (is (= 1 @calls))\n   258\t      (is (= :dao.stream.waitset/invalid-answer\n   259\t             (:status (first (:woken check)))))\n   260\t      (is (= [] (get-in check [:waitset :waiting])))\n   261\t      (is (zero? advances))))\n   262\t  (testing \"a nil answer\"\n   263\t    (let [entry {:reason :put :my/ref :r :my/value :payload}\n   264\t          {:keys [handle calls]} (answering-writer nil)\n   265\t          {:keys [check advances]} (check-one entry handle)]\n   266\t      (is (= 1 @calls) \"the append was attempted once\")\n   267\t      (is (= :dao.stream.waitset/invalid-answer\n   268\t             (:status (first (:woken check)))))\n   269\t      (is (= [] (get-in check [:waitset :waiting])))\n   270\t      (is (zero? advances))))\n   271\t  (testing \"a handle that fails its protocol throws into the same diagnostic\"\n   272\t    (let [entry {:reason :next :my/ref :r}\n   273\t          ;; A truthy :stream that satisfies no reader protocol: the poll\n   274\t          ;; dispatch fails at the host, and the entry cannot be trusted\n   275\t          ;; to poll again.\n   276\t          {:keys [check advances]} (check-one entry :not-a-handle)\n   277\t          wake (first (:woken check))]\n   278\t      (is (= 1 (count (:woken check))))\n   279\t      (is (= entry (:entry wake)))\n   280\t      (is (= :dao.stream.waitset/invalid-answer (:status wake)))\n   281\t      (is (= [] (get-in check [:waitset :waiting])))\n   282\t      (is (= [] (:store check)))\n   283\t      (is (zero? advances)))))\n   284\t\n   285\t\n   286\t(deftest park-is-total-over-missing-and-nil-waiting\n   287\t  (let [entry {:reason :next :my/ref :r}\n   288\t        entry-b {:reason :next :my/ref :r2}]\n   289\t    (testing \"a waitset without :waiting parks onto a fresh vector\"\n   290\t      (is (= {:waiting [entry]} (waitset/park {} entry)))\n   291\t      (is (= {:waiting [entry]} (waitset/park {:waiting nil} entry))))\n   292\t    (testing \"park order — wake order among co-waiters — is preserved\"\n   293\t      (is (= {:waiting [entry entry-b]}\n   294\t             (-> {:waiting nil}\n   295\t                 (waitset/park entry)\n   296\t                 (waitset/park entry-b)))))))\n   297\t\n   298\t\n   299\t(deftest undeclared-outcome-is-terminal-under-its-own-keyword\n   300\t  (let [rogue :dao.stream/quantum-flux]\n   301\t    (is (not (contains? stream/outcomes-next rogue)))\n   302\t    (is (not (contains? stream/outcomes-append rogue)))\n   303\t    (testing \"for a :next entry\"\n   304\t      (let [entry {:reason :next :my/ref :r}\n   305\t            {:keys [check advances]}\n   306\t            (check-one entry (:handle (scripted-reader rogue)))\n   307\t            wake (first (:woken check))]\n   308\t        (is (= 1 (count (:woken check))))\n   309\t        (is (= rogue (:status wake)))\n   310\t        (is (= rogue (:value wake)))\n   311\t        (is (not (contains? wake :cursor)))\n   312\t        (is (= [] (get-in check [:waitset :waiting])))\n   313\t        (is (zero? advances) \"no cursor was returned, so no write-back\")))\n   314\t    (testing \"for a :put entry\"\n   315\t      (let [entry {:reason :put :my/ref :r :my/value :payload}\n   316\t            {:keys [check advances]}\n   317\t            (check-one entry (:handle (scripted-writer rogue)))]\n   318\t        (is (= 1 (count (:woken check))))\n   319\t        (is (= rogue (:status (first (:woken check)))))\n   320\t        (is (= rogue (:value (first (:woken check)))))\n   321\t        (is (= [] (get-in check [:waitset :waiting])))\n   322\t        (is (zero? advances))))))\n   323\t\n   324\t\n   325\t(deftest woken-results-carry-what-the-poll-yielded\n   326\t  (testing \"a reader's ok carries the value and its successor cursor\"\n   327\t    (let [entry {:reason :next :my/ref :r}\n   328\t          result (:check (check-one entry\n   329\t                                    (:handle (scripted-reader\n   330\t                                              :dao.stream/ok))))]\n   331\t      (is (= [{:entry entry :status :ok :value :sent :cursor {:pos 1}}]\n   332\t             (:woken result)))))\n   333\t  (testing \"end carries no value and no cursor\"\n   334\t    (let [entry {:reason :next :my/ref :r}\n   335\t          result (:check (check-one entry\n   336\t                                    (:handle (scripted-reader\n   337\t                                              :dao.stream/end))))]\n   338\t      (is (= [{:entry entry :status :end :value nil}] (:woken result)))))\n   339\t  (testing \"a reader failure resolves under its own keyword\"\n   340\t    (let [entry {:reason :next :my/ref :r}\n   341\t          result (:check (check-one entry\n   342\t                                    (:handle (scripted-reader\n   343\t                                              :dao.stream/transport-error))))]\n   344\t      (is (= [{:entry entry\n   345\t               :status :dao.stream/transport-error\n   346\t               :value :dao.stream/transport-error}]\n   347\t             (:woken result)))))\n   348\t  (testing \"a writer's ok resolves with the appended value and no cursor\"\n   349\t    (let [entry {:reason :put :my/ref :r :my/value :payload}\n   350\t          result (:check (check-one entry\n   351\t                                    (:handle (scripted-writer\n   352\t                                              :dao.stream/ok))))]\n   353\t      (is (= [{:entry entry :status :ok :value :payload}]\n   354\t             (:woken result))))))\n   355\t\n   356\t\n   357\t(deftest shared-cursor-wakes-co-waiters-on-distinct-values-in-wait-set-order\n   358\t  (let [h (ring-handle)\n   359\t        _ (doseq [v [:a :b :c]] (stream/append! h v))\n   360\t        entry-a {:reason :next :my/ref :shared :my/tag :first}\n   361\t        entry-b {:reason :next :my/ref :shared :my/tag :second}\n   362\t        store (alist-store [[:shared [h (cursor h :dao.stream/oldest)]]])\n   363\t        result (waitset/check (-> (waitset/empty-waitset)\n   364\t                                  (waitset/park entry-a)\n   365\t                                  (waitset/park entry-b))\n   366\t                              (alist-resolver)\n   367\t                              store)]\n   368\t    ;; Wait-set order is wake order, and one cursor wakes two distinct\n   369\t    ;; values: b resolved against the store a's write-back advanced.\n   370\t    (is (= [:first :second] (mapv (comp :my/tag :entry) (:woken result))))\n   371\t    (is (= [:a :b] (mapv :value (:woken result))))\n   372\t    (is (= [:ok :ok] (mapv :status (:woken result))))\n   373\t    ;; Entries are returned exactly as stored.\n   374\t    (is (= entry-a (:entry (first (:woken result)))))\n   375\t    (is (= entry-b (:entry (second (:woken result)))))\n   376\t    ;; Both write-backs landed: the store ends at b's successor.\n   377\t    (is (= (:cursor (second (:woken result)))\n   378\t           (alist-cursor (:store result) :shared)))\n   379\t    (is (= [] (get-in result [:waitset :waiting])))))\n   380\t\n   381\t\n   382\t(deftest parked-writer-retries-by-appending\n   383\t  (let [{:keys [handle calls]} (full-once-writer)\n   384\t        advances (atom 0)\n   385\t        entry {:reason :put :my/ref :w :my/value :payload}\n   386\t        resolver (fixture-resolver handle advances)\n   387\t        first-check (waitset/check (waitset/park (waitset/empty-waitset) entry)\n   388\t                                   resolver\n   389\t                                   [:no-store-motion])]\n   390\t    ;; Exactly one append per poll: the first sweep appended once and the\n   391\t    ;; handle answered full, so the entry is retained as stored.\n   392\t    (is (= 1 @calls))\n   393\t    (is (zero? @advances) \"a writer's poll never moves the store\")\n   394\t    (is (= [] (:woken first-check)))\n   395\t    (is (= [entry] (get-in first-check [:waitset :waiting])))\n   396\t    ;; Threading the returned waitset and store retries by appending — no\n   397\t    ;; polled state discarded — and resolves the writer with its host\n   398\t    ;; value.\n   399\t    (let [second-check (waitset/check (:waitset first-check)\n   400\t                                      resolver\n   401\t                                      (:store first-check))]\n   402\t      (is (= 2 @calls))\n   403\t      (is (= [{:entry entry :status :ok :value :payload}]\n   404\t             (:woken second-check)))\n   405\t      (is (= [] (get-in second-check [:waitset :waiting]))))))\n   406\t\n   407\t\n   408\t(deftest gap-recovery-wakes-co-waiters-from-the-recovery-position\n   409\t  (let [h (ring-handle 2)\n   410\t        _ (do (stream/append! h :old)\n   411\t              (stream/append! h :new))\n   412\t        stale (cursor h :dao.stream/oldest)\n   413\t        _ (stream/append! h :newest)   ;; evicts :old at position 0\n   414\t        entry-a {:reason :next :my/ref :shared :my/tag :first}\n   415\t        entry-b {:reason :next :my/ref :shared :my/tag :second}\n   416\t        store (alist-store [[:shared [h stale]]])\n   417\t        result (waitset/check (-> (waitset/empty-waitset)\n   418\t                                  (waitset/park entry-a)\n   419\t                                  (waitset/park entry-b))\n   420\t                              (alist-resolver)\n   421\t                              store)\n   422\t        [a b] (:woken result)]\n   423\t    ;; a wakes first, with the gap and its recovery cursor: the earliest\n   424\t    ;; retained position.\n   425\t    (is (= :first (:my/tag (:entry a))))\n   426\t    (is (= :dao.stream/gap (:status a)))\n   427\t    (is (= :dao.stream/gap (:value a)))\n   428\t    (is (= 1 (:dao.stream.ringbuffer/position (:cursor a))))\n   429\t    ;; b resolved against a's write-back in the same call and read the\n   430\t    ;; earliest retained value.\n   431\t    (is (= :second (:my/tag (:entry b))))\n   432\t    (is (= :ok (:status b)))\n   433\t    (is (= :new (:value b)))\n   434\t    (is (= 2 (:dao.stream.ringbuffer/position (:cursor b))))\n   435\t    ;; The store ends at b's successor.\n   436\t    (is (= 2 (:dao.stream.ringbuffer/position\n   437\t               (alist-